WEBVTT

00:01.290 --> 00:08.290
<i>Can you imagine a life where you 
can't even touch the person you love?</i>

00:09.150 --> 00:14.140
<i>The curse the witch laid upon him caused 
him to take the lives of any he touched.</i>

00:14.760 --> 00:19.080
<i>His own mother distanced herself from him,
 his friends called him a monster...</i>

00:19.080 --> 00:20.460
<i>Even people he'd never met spoke of him as</i>

00:20.460 --> 00:23.510
<i>"death incarnate that dwells in the forest."</i>

00:24.150 --> 00:29.180
<i>And yet, he doesn't feel 
the least bit lonely.</i>

00:35.430 --> 00:37.870
Good morning. Breakfast is ready.

00:47.670 --> 00:50.010
Alice, why don't you take a break?

00:50.010 --> 00:51.960
I'll do the cleaning for once.

00:51.960 --> 00:52.900
But...

00:53.380 --> 00:55.300
Here, just leave it to me.

00:59.540 --> 01:01.310
Where did you pull that out from?

01:01.310 --> 01:03.790
No, I mean, go take a rest!

01:03.790 --> 01:05.540
There's nothing else for me to do.

01:05.540 --> 01:07.860
Then relax!

01:07.860 --> 01:09.790
I know. Don't you have any hobbies?

01:10.440 --> 01:11.500
You're my hobby.

01:11.500 --> 01:13.960
Then something you like?

01:14.280 --> 01:15.720
You're what I like.

01:16.120 --> 01:17.860
O-Oh... huh!

02:49.020 --> 02:51.980
Episode 15
The Duke, Alice, and the Spectral Bride

02:52.240 --> 02:55.840
Listen, Alice. Listen!

02:55.840 --> 03:00.320
The person you love is about 
to come out of the next room.

03:00.320 --> 03:01.660
Make sure not to run into them.

03:02.250 --> 03:03.030
Alice!

03:03.410 --> 03:05.530
I'm glad I didn't run into you.

03:05.530 --> 03:08.090
You were in the library this late?

03:08.090 --> 03:09.000
Yeah.

03:09.340 --> 03:11.460
I was really curious 
about this business card.

03:11.760 --> 03:15.290
So I was trying to look into what an 
octopus could have to do with witches...

03:15.290 --> 03:16.920
But I didn't get anywhere.

03:17.200 --> 03:19.080
Oh, I see.

03:19.080 --> 03:21.040
Will you take a shower?

03:21.040 --> 03:23.580
I haven't taken one myself yet, 
so it would be perfect timing.

03:23.580 --> 03:25.810
Why do you think we'd take one together?!

03:25.810 --> 03:28.600
Aw, look at the two of you having fun.

03:32.060 --> 03:35.630
You, know, Alice, I've been wondering...

03:36.020 --> 03:38.240
Do you see them?

03:38.240 --> 03:39.490
See what?

03:39.490 --> 03:40.740
Ghosts!

03:41.240 --> 03:44.740
I felt like maybe you did when that 
thing with McFarlane happened.

03:45.270 --> 03:46.810
I do not.

03:46.810 --> 03:48.070
You're lying!

03:48.070 --> 03:51.710
You're just pretending not to 
see them so I won't get scared!

03:52.040 --> 03:54.510
You're all I see.

03:54.510 --> 03:57.120
Really?!

03:57.120 --> 03:59.550
I mean, that makes me happy! 
But that wasn't what I meant!

04:00.540 --> 04:05.910
I saw you talking by yourself last night...

04:07.370 --> 04:10.770
Do you know anyone who looks like me, then?

04:11.480 --> 04:13.270
Her name would be Sharon.

04:13.270 --> 04:17.770
"Morning! The sun's shining so 
bright today! Mommy feels great!"

04:18.660 --> 04:20.730
That's how she talks.

04:21.840 --> 04:23.260
<i>So cute...</i>

04:24.890 --> 04:27.730
I'll be fine. So I want 
you to tell me the truth.

04:27.730 --> 04:31.440
Alice, you see ghosts, don't you?

04:32.880 --> 04:34.260
I do not.

04:34.260 --> 04:35.750
You're so stubborn!

04:35.750 --> 04:37.520
I don't see them,

04:38.600 --> 04:40.770
but it's possible that there's been

04:40.770 --> 04:43.370
a ghost in the mansion dressed like 
a spectral bride since yesterday.

04:43.370 --> 04:44.800
You do see them, then!

04:44.800 --> 04:47.060
Is she s-saying anything?

04:47.060 --> 04:50.010
Like that she wants revenge 
or has unfinished business?

04:50.260 --> 04:54.080
I married the man I loved,

04:54.080 --> 04:58.360
but on the day of the wedding, 
this was the ring I got.

04:58.890 --> 05:00.930
I got so mad I lost control of myself,

05:00.930 --> 05:02.740
and then I fell down the stairs and died!

05:03.090 --> 05:06.080
That's a sad way to go.

05:06.080 --> 05:07.700
You're talking with it right now, aren't you?

05:08.320 --> 05:10.910
I don't see them, 
but they're usually like that.

05:10.910 --> 05:13.330
You're acting really silly 
today, and it's very cute!

05:14.930 --> 05:16.540
How about one of these?

05:17.240 --> 05:21.750
I don't know who they belong to, but they've 
been in the mansion for a long time.

05:22.400 --> 05:24.150
There are a lot of different sizes.

05:24.150 --> 05:26.100
She can take the one she likes.

05:26.510 --> 05:29.970
Maybe if she finds the perfect ring,
 she'll be able to go to heaven.

05:30.620 --> 05:32.490
Can I really take one?

05:32.490 --> 05:33.930
Yes, if you like it.

05:34.320 --> 05:36.420
You're just talking to a ghost now.

05:36.420 --> 05:37.690
But I don't see them.

05:38.870 --> 05:43.130
He should've measured her ring size.

05:44.000 --> 05:46.230
Perhaps it was a surprise?

05:46.230 --> 05:51.020
Sure, but you can wrap a string around her 
finger while she's asleep or something.

05:55.590 --> 05:57.410
<i>What's wrong with these two?</i>

06:00.710 --> 06:02.930
I'm getting jealous.

06:02.930 --> 06:04.670
Lend me your body for a little.

06:08.890 --> 06:10.510
Alice?

06:11.690 --> 06:17.210
Your Grace, I can't control myself anymore.

06:18.100 --> 06:20.880
Maybe there's a spot where 
it's safe to touch me.

06:21.530 --> 06:24.190
Why don't we find out together?

06:26.690 --> 06:28.250
N-No!

06:28.250 --> 06:32.030
I don't think I can control myself!

06:32.030 --> 06:33.530
I'm sorry, Alice!

06:34.540 --> 06:36.500
Why did he run away?

06:36.930 --> 06:39.800
My darling's the only one for me.

06:40.450 --> 06:43.290
I'll wait until he's dead.

06:43.290 --> 06:45.460
You'll wait all that time?

06:45.900 --> 06:48.520
Yes. I really do love him.

06:48.520 --> 06:51.430
And looking back, I think 
I can forgive him for the ring.

06:52.620 --> 06:57.440
And I need to apologize for dying 
so suddenly and leaving him alone.

06:57.440 --> 07:00.180
I guess I made too big a deal out of it.

07:00.880 --> 07:04.120
I'm satisfied now. I'll just move on.

07:04.120 --> 07:06.020
You can have this.

07:09.200 --> 07:11.450
Um, please find happiness.

07:12.140 --> 07:13.810
You too.

07:21.460 --> 07:23.390
Will they come today, you think?

07:24.340 --> 07:29.090
The owner of this business card was 
supposed to come in a few days.

07:29.350 --> 07:31.840
That's what Daleth said.

07:31.840 --> 07:34.310
But I need to drive them away when they come!

07:34.310 --> 07:35.850
You're sure?

07:37.310 --> 07:39.810
Well, I'd love to break the curse.

07:40.200 --> 07:44.770
But if I end up owing Daleth a favor 
over it, I'll have to do what she wants.

07:45.240 --> 07:51.530
I want you to ask Zain to 
use his time magic again.

07:52.570 --> 07:56.880
I promised Zain, so I can't 
tell you the details.

07:57.210 --> 07:59.680
But I don't want to cause problems for him.

07:59.680 --> 08:00.500
Don't worry.

08:00.840 --> 08:04.410
No matter what kind of witch 
it is, I'll protect you.

08:04.410 --> 08:05.880
How brave.

08:06.270 --> 08:07.250
Let me thank you by...

08:07.250 --> 08:08.820
Keep your clothes on!

08:08.820 --> 08:10.380
Are you psychic?

08:13.600 --> 08:15.390
It seems someone's here.

08:20.230 --> 08:21.810
I-It's time...

08:22.780 --> 08:24.550
Daleth told me to come here.

08:24.550 --> 08:26.520
Is this the place?

08:26.520 --> 08:28.490
U-Um, it's, uh...

08:28.490 --> 08:30.400
Is this your business card?

08:30.400 --> 08:34.270
Oh, great! I finally made it...

08:39.720 --> 08:41.290
W-Water...

08:41.900 --> 08:44.750
Put me in salt water, fast!

08:45.930 --> 08:48.460
Thanks so much!

08:49.110 --> 08:53.520
It's been so long since I've been on land,
 and I kind of forgot how it works.

08:53.520 --> 08:55.930
I almost dried up!

08:56.490 --> 08:58.450
I wasn't really thinking 
when I saved you but...

08:58.450 --> 09:01.410
You're the witch that's good 
with breaking curses, right?

09:01.410 --> 09:03.990
Yes. I'm Amelia.

09:03.990 --> 09:08.890
I'm not so much a witch... as I 
am an octopus born with magic.

09:11.130 --> 09:13.490
Daleth told me about you.

09:13.790 --> 09:17.950
A curse that kills just by touching, right?

09:18.510 --> 09:21.290
I've broken a similar curse in the past.

09:21.290 --> 09:23.160
I won't know until I try, but...

09:25.130 --> 09:27.620
I might be able to break it for you!

09:31.590 --> 09:35.050
Um... I hate to say this after 
you came all the way here.

09:35.930 --> 09:37.510
But I'm thinking of saying no.

09:38.830 --> 09:41.020
I don't want to owe Daleth anything.

09:41.020 --> 09:42.970
It'll cause problems for a friend of mine.

09:42.970 --> 09:46.440
Humans are always so loyal.

09:46.440 --> 09:48.190
You're such fun creatures!

09:48.650 --> 09:51.450
You've dealt with humans in the past?

09:51.450 --> 09:56.120
Yes. I even married an 
unusual man a decade ago.

09:56.120 --> 09:56.900
Married?!

09:57.260 --> 10:00.100
Well, it was only a formality.

10:00.940 --> 10:03.400
I was so bored back then

10:03.400 --> 10:05.170
that I would take the form of a huge octopus

10:05.170 --> 10:07.330
and attack the cargo that ships were carrying.

10:07.700 --> 10:11.540
But one day I attacked an armed pirate ship.

10:13.450 --> 10:16.050
I guess this is it for me.

10:18.770 --> 10:20.570
What is this?

10:20.570 --> 10:22.110
Let me out!

10:24.170 --> 10:25.730
Stay put.

10:25.730 --> 10:27.730
I won't hurt you.

10:28.960 --> 10:31.840
He'd happened to be aboard that day.

10:31.840 --> 10:35.570
He hid me among the other 
cargo so I could escape.

10:35.570 --> 10:38.200
Th-Thank you for helping me.

10:38.500 --> 10:40.030
Don't worry about it.

10:40.030 --> 10:43.700
What could be more entertaining 
than talking with an octopus witch?

10:43.700 --> 10:45.160
Is that how it works?

10:50.250 --> 10:51.480
You got a boyfriend?

10:52.880 --> 10:55.880
It all happened so fast after that...

10:56.140 --> 10:58.800
We exchanged rings, 
though they were cheap ones...

10:58.800 --> 11:02.040
And he went back to the city, and I the sea.

11:02.410 --> 11:06.350
I doubt he remembers, but for me,
 it's a wonderful memory.

11:06.900 --> 11:10.560
I've never seen him again, 
but I still love him.

11:10.560 --> 11:12.560
That's so romantic!

11:12.810 --> 11:13.680
Right?

11:13.680 --> 11:17.290
I'm not like the pretty 
mermaids in the fairy tales!

11:17.290 --> 11:19.290
Who knows what about me he liked?!

11:19.290 --> 11:20.990
She d-disappeared?

11:20.990 --> 11:22.970
No, it's camouflage.

11:22.970 --> 11:26.430
She's changed the color of her 
body to match her surroundings.

11:26.430 --> 11:28.120
So we can't see how embarrassed she is?

11:31.770 --> 11:35.760
I know you're bothered by 
what Daleth said, but...

11:35.760 --> 11:38.300
I can't promise I'll be 
able to break the curse.

11:38.300 --> 11:42.820
Why not let me try before 
deciding what you'll do?

11:42.820 --> 11:43.550
But...

11:44.030 --> 11:46.270
Are you that scared of Daleth?

11:46.270 --> 11:47.760
I am!

11:47.760 --> 11:52.270
She's got that scary mask and I can 
never tell what she's thinking!

11:52.880 --> 11:55.550
Well, she can be difficult.

11:55.550 --> 11:57.150
She doesn't know how to express herself,

11:57.150 --> 11:58.400
and makes her own life harder.

11:58.980 --> 12:04.450
But she's not a bad girl. 
Don't hate her too much.

12:04.450 --> 12:06.630
But she rules the Witches' World!

12:06.630 --> 12:11.620
That's a witch thing. 
I'm an octopus. I don't care.

12:11.620 --> 12:15.900
She only ended up ruling because everybody
 wanted her to, and she couldn't say no.

12:17.030 --> 12:20.700
First, let's see if we can break your curse.

12:20.700 --> 12:24.670
Or else what did I risk 
my life coming here for?

12:24.670 --> 12:25.890
True...

12:26.360 --> 12:29.260
How likely do you think it is 
you'll be able to break it?

12:29.260 --> 12:32.290
It depends on how powerful the 
witch who laid the curse is.

12:32.290 --> 12:35.920
But from past experience, 
I'd say there's an 80% chance.

12:37.940 --> 12:39.320
80%...

12:43.010 --> 12:49.200
If I break the curse, will I be able 
to put a ring on Alice's finger?

12:51.150 --> 12:52.660
Of course.

12:53.960 --> 12:55.370
Then please, help me.

12:55.370 --> 12:58.630
If it works, I'll make it 
up to Daleth some other way.

12:59.340 --> 13:01.380
Great!

13:03.090 --> 13:08.140
Let's get you turned back into 
a normal human right away, then.

13:15.390 --> 13:17.350
Here I go, poor cursed boy.

13:20.170 --> 13:21.860
Don't dodge!

13:21.860 --> 13:23.530
Sorry! Years of habit!

13:23.830 --> 13:26.800
But it's dangerous to touch me!

13:26.800 --> 13:29.030
Witches and octopuses are 
both living creatures.

13:29.030 --> 13:31.100
I'm a pro, okay?

13:31.100 --> 13:36.000
A curse clings to the 
sufferer's body like a film.

13:37.830 --> 13:41.370
If you want to break the curse,
 you just rip it off.

13:41.370 --> 13:43.420
I don't need to touch you.

13:43.740 --> 13:46.390
Want to see my power for yourself?

13:51.400 --> 13:54.050
What? Fish?

13:54.050 --> 13:56.820
The sea is the source of all life.

13:57.260 --> 14:01.190
I can call upon the great 
power that dwells in the sea.

14:02.340 --> 14:04.340
I can breathe and talk.

14:04.340 --> 14:06.700
Wow! Is this your magic?

14:06.700 --> 14:08.690
Wow, you're a genius!

14:10.040 --> 14:11.330
Please don't disappear, though!

14:11.330 --> 14:12.620
It makes it hard to compliment you!

14:15.920 --> 14:18.110
Is it alive?

14:19.280 --> 14:22.750
The fish are all so cute!

14:24.060 --> 14:26.800
They're so cute! And so are you!

14:26.800 --> 14:29.220
I'm impressed that you can cry underwater...

14:30.730 --> 14:32.270
Look, Your Grace.

14:32.270 --> 14:33.180
The hallway, too!

14:33.770 --> 14:35.690
And there's a whale outside, too!

14:36.390 --> 14:39.710
My magic covers this whole mansion.

14:39.710 --> 14:41.750
Why not take a walk?

14:41.750 --> 14:42.900
Yay!

14:44.850 --> 14:46.700
He looks like a good kid.

14:46.700 --> 14:49.400
Why was he cursed, I wonder?

14:52.700 --> 14:56.120
I'm looking down at the 
mansion... It's so strange.

14:56.480 --> 14:58.820
Look, Alice! There's a 
dolphin right next to me!

14:58.820 --> 15:00.830
How cute!

15:01.700 --> 15:03.070
This is fun.

15:03.070 --> 15:06.700
I've never seen fish swimming so close to me.

15:06.700 --> 15:07.800
Me either.

15:12.220 --> 15:16.260
It's like I'm on an undersea date with you.

15:16.260 --> 15:19.050
A-Aw, a date?

15:23.520 --> 15:28.510
<i>Let's walk through the sea together</i>

15:28.510 --> 15:33.180
<i>Let's swim under the sky</i>

15:33.180 --> 15:37.640
<i>A fantastic world beneath shining waves</i>

15:37.640 --> 15:42.460
<i>The fish are dreaming shining dreams</i>

15:42.460 --> 15:46.880
<i>The dolphins, the jellyfish, the sunfish</i>

15:46.880 --> 15:51.790
<i>The angelfish are cute too, but</i>

15:51.790 --> 15:57.950
<i>You're my mermaid after all</i>

15:57.950 --> 16:05.730
<i>I'm not just a maid, I'm your </i>mer<i>maid!</i>

16:05.730 --> 16:07.310
Let's see what's down below, too.

16:07.310 --> 16:08.440
Oh, okay.

16:10.940 --> 16:12.570
A tiger shark!

16:12.570 --> 16:14.110
The pattern is so cute!

16:14.110 --> 16:16.550
And that's an elephant shark next to you!

16:16.550 --> 16:18.010
See how its nose is like an elephant's trunk?

16:18.010 --> 16:18.620
Yes.

16:19.380 --> 16:23.920
It's so strange, seeing all these fish from 
different parts of the world in one place.

16:23.920 --> 16:25.830
You know a lot about fish, Your Grace.

16:25.830 --> 16:30.050
Ever since I came here, I've always 
been alone when it was time to play.

16:30.750 --> 16:34.760
There wasn't much to do but draw 
pictures out of the encyclopedias.

16:38.420 --> 16:40.650
The deep sea fish are all so unique, too.

16:40.650 --> 16:42.480
Yes, it's kind of cute.

16:42.820 --> 16:44.090
Did you have fun?

16:44.090 --> 16:45.370
Yes, a lot!

16:45.370 --> 16:47.160
It was a wonderful time.

16:47.160 --> 16:48.630
I'm glad.

16:48.630 --> 16:51.190
Now, may I get to work?

16:51.190 --> 16:53.420
Yeah. Sorry for getting too excited.

16:53.420 --> 16:55.620
Don't move. Put your hands out.

16:55.620 --> 16:56.430
Okay.

17:04.400 --> 17:05.830
Amelia?

17:05.830 --> 17:07.360
I'm fine.

17:07.360 --> 17:10.700
But what happened in your past?

17:11.730 --> 17:16.140
I can see why Daleth came to me.

17:16.140 --> 17:22.380
I only know of one witch in all of history 
who could lay such an evil curse!

17:27.360 --> 17:30.170
Will Amelia be able to break that curse?

17:30.860 --> 17:33.850
Well, I don't expect much.

17:34.860 --> 17:38.250
<i>Zain, don't make a kid 
carry such heavy stuff!</i>

17:38.250 --> 17:40.280
<i>I'm carrying more than you!</i>

17:40.280 --> 17:44.220
<i>Don't act like a kid only when it helps you!</i>

17:44.690 --> 17:45.960
Gemini...

17:46.990 --> 17:48.430
The constellation of twins.

17:49.710 --> 17:51.490
Wh-What do you mean?

17:51.490 --> 17:53.890
You know the witch who cursed me?

17:53.890 --> 17:55.170
Just watch.

17:56.690 --> 17:58.020
This is...

17:58.020 --> 18:00.060
The curse placed on you.

18:00.060 --> 18:01.640
Even if I try to rip it off,

18:03.050 --> 18:05.560
it clings right to you.

18:05.930 --> 18:07.890
Amelia, you don't look well...

18:08.370 --> 18:11.210
Its evil power is affecting me.

18:11.210 --> 18:13.910
Don't bother me, Flapjack.

18:15.270 --> 18:19.150
I heard she was dead, but I guess 
I still can't break the curse.

18:19.150 --> 18:21.320
Who is this witch?

18:21.950 --> 18:26.580
Sade, Daleth's twin sister.

18:27.530 --> 18:28.790
Sister?

18:29.160 --> 18:31.030
You can't think of any reason she did this?

18:31.030 --> 18:31.930
No!

18:31.930 --> 18:34.750
This is the first time I've 
heard Daleth had a twin.

18:36.310 --> 18:42.100
<i>Were the two women in habits that the 
logbook spoke of Daleth and Sade?</i>

18:42.970 --> 18:45.720
<i>But what were they doing there that day?</i>

18:45.980 --> 18:51.100
<i>So the reason Daleth wants time 
magic has something to do Sade?</i>

18:51.600 --> 18:53.930
<i>Does she want to bring her back to life?</i>

18:54.590 --> 18:56.000
<i>I don't know...</i>

18:56.000 --> 18:58.090
Did I say a little too much?

18:58.090 --> 18:59.900
Daleth will get mad at me.

19:01.300 --> 19:04.120
That curse is more powerful than I am.

19:04.120 --> 19:07.210
I'm sorry, but I don't think I can break it.

19:07.700 --> 19:10.540
How did such a powerful witch die?

19:10.820 --> 19:13.500
I don't know...

19:14.890 --> 19:16.030
The fish...

19:16.030 --> 19:16.970
What's happening?

19:18.160 --> 19:19.100
Amelia?

19:19.100 --> 19:21.070
I'm sorry, I can't keep this up.

19:21.070 --> 19:23.430
Carry me to the sea!

19:23.430 --> 19:24.650
Please!

19:24.650 --> 19:26.220
H-How...?

19:29.700 --> 19:32.340
I'm sorry I couldn't help.

19:32.340 --> 19:36.360
It's okay. I'm sorry we couldn't 
do more to welcome you.

19:36.710 --> 19:39.530
I hope you can see your 
husband again someday.

19:39.750 --> 19:42.490
Oh, thanks.

19:43.940 --> 19:45.750
Be well, you two.

19:45.750 --> 19:48.050
I'm looking forward to seeing you again.

19:48.050 --> 19:49.180
Oh, yeah.

19:49.490 --> 19:52.460
I'm not sure where to look 
when I'm speaking, though.

19:56.170 --> 19:57.490
Hey, Alice.

19:57.820 --> 20:00.780
Let's go see Cuff and Zain soon.

20:01.190 --> 20:03.760
I want to talk to them about Daleth and Sade.

20:03.760 --> 20:07.890
It's rare for you to want to go into town.

20:08.520 --> 20:10.480
If you want tickets to the circus,

20:10.910 --> 20:12.970
Cuff gave me some.

20:12.970 --> 20:15.100
You're putting stuff there again?

20:16.190 --> 20:17.860
When the curse is broken...

20:18.380 --> 20:20.570
I want to go to all kinds of places with you.

20:21.120 --> 20:26.030
I only know what lies beyond 
that horizon from books.

20:26.790 --> 20:30.000
I want to see things with my own eyes.

20:30.670 --> 20:32.460
Where do you want to go, Alice?

20:32.830 --> 20:37.420
Hmm... the place I was born, 
where I lived with my mother.

20:38.390 --> 20:41.290
I've only got scattered memories of it left,

20:41.290 --> 20:43.380
but there was a big garden,

20:43.380 --> 20:47.430
and my mother taught me 
all about flowers there.

20:48.030 --> 20:52.890
I'd love for you to see 
it someday, Your Grace.

20:53.240 --> 20:54.440
Let's go, then!

20:54.440 --> 20:55.400
Let's promise!

20:55.720 --> 20:58.360
We can take Rob and Viola, and Cuff and Zain.

20:59.020 --> 21:02.820
I'd love it if Mom, Dad, 
and Walter came, too.

21:03.090 --> 21:03.930
Right?

21:03.930 --> 21:07.390
When the curse is broken, we'll all 
go to where you grew up together.

21:07.390 --> 21:08.280
It's a promise!

21:09.930 --> 21:11.140
<i>Together...</i>

21:12.380 --> 21:18.460
<i>How happy would I be if I could still 
be with you when the curse is broken?</i>

21:20.920 --> 21:21.810
Yes.

21:22.660 --> 21:24.520
Let's promise.

21:24.520 --> 21:25.280
Yeah.

21:28.530 --> 21:30.790
The sea's so cold at night.

21:30.790 --> 21:32.770
Want to get naked and warm each other up?

21:33.160 --> 21:34.960
I'd rather not...

23:07.120 --> 23:10.260
Hey, you're married, right boss?

23:10.260 --> 23:11.700
What's she like?

23:12.360 --> 23:13.690
She's beautiful.

23:14.120 --> 23:16.340
She's easily embarrassed and 
likes to hide herself...

23:16.340 --> 23:19.210
And she's got hands this big, and eight legs!

23:19.210 --> 23:21.700
You made the last half of that up!

23:21.700 --> 23:24.710
We've lived apart for 10 years, though.

23:25.510 --> 23:27.350
I miss her...

23:27.350 --> 23:29.540
I'm gonna go clean the toilets.

23:29.540 --> 23:31.490
Don't freak the kid out like that?

23:31.490 --> 23:31.970
Huh?

23:34.970 --> 23:40.250
The Duke of Death and His Maid
The Duke, Alice, and Circus 101

23:35.660 --> 23:39.360
"The Duke, Alice, and Circus 101."
